KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty-pack decltype resolves: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A variadic forwarding helper whose trailing-return decltype contains a pack
expansion f(a...), deduced with an EMPTY pack, should collapse to f() and
resolve.  An empty deduced parameter pack is not recorded during deduction, so
the trailing-return pack expansion is not collapsed and decltype(invk(...))
fails vacuously.  Affects both the plain and forwarding-cast forms.  Flip to
CORE once an empty deduced pack is recorded.  N5008 [temp.variadic]/5,7.
